#: aequilibrae/parameters.py:12
msgid ""
"Global parameters module.\n"
"\n"
"    Parameters are used in many procedures, and are often defined in the ``parameters.yml`` file ONLY.\n"
"\n"
"    Parameters are organized in the following groups:\n"
"\n"
"    * assignment\n"
"    * distribution\n"
"    * network\n"
"      * links\n"
"      * modes\n"
"      * nodes\n"
"      * osm\n"
"      * gmns\n"
"    * osm\n"
"    * system\n"
"\n"
"    Please observe that OSM information handled on network is not the same on the OSM group.\n"
"\n"
"    .. code-block:: python\n"
"\n"
"        >>> from aequilibrae.parameters import Parameters\n"
"\n"
"        >>> project = Project()\n"
"        >>> project.new(project_path)\n"
"\n"
"        >>> p = Parameters()\n"
"\n"
"        >>> p.parameters['system']['logging_directory'] =  \"/path_to/other_logging_directory\"\n"
"        >>> p.parameters['osm']['overpass_endpoint'] = \"http://192.168.0.110:32780/api\"\n"
"        >>> p.parameters['osm']['max_query_area_size'] = 10000000000\n"
"        >>> p.parameters['osm']['sleeptime'] = 0\n"
"        >>> p.write_back()\n"
"\n"
"        >>> # You can also restore the software default values\n"
"        >>> p.restore_default()\n"
"\n"
"        >>> project.close()\n"
"    "
msgstr ""
"Módulo de parámetros globales.\n"
"\n"
"    Los parámetros se utilizan en muchos procedimientos y, a menudo, se definen ÚNICAMENTE en el archivo "
"``parameters.yml``.\n"
"\n"
"    Los parámetros están organizados en los siguientes grupos:\n"
"\n"
"    * tarea\n"
"    * distribución\n"
"    * red\n"
"      * enlaces\n"
"      * modos\n"
"      * nodos\n"
"      * osm\n"
"      * gmns\n"
"    * osm\n"
"    * sistema\n"
"\n"
"    Tenga en cuenta que la información de OSM manejada en la red no es la misma en el grupo de OSM.\n"
"\n"
"    .. bloque de código:: python\n"
"\n"
"        >>> desde aequilibrae.parameters importar parámetros\n"
"\n"
"        >>> proyecto = Proyecto()\n"
"        >>> proyecto.nuevo(ruta_proyecto)\n"
"\n"
"        >>> p = Parámetros()\n"
"\n"
"        >>> p.parameters['system']['logging_directory'] = \"/ruta_al/otro_directorio_logging\"\n"
"        >>> p.parameters['osm']['overpass_endpoint'] = \"http://192.168.0.110:32780/api\"\n"
"        >>> p.parameters['osm']['max_query_area_size'] = 10000000000\n"
"        >>> p.parameters['osm']['hora de dormir'] = 0\n"
"        >>> p.write_back()\n"
"\n"
"        >>> # También puedes restaurar los valores predeterminados del software.\n"
"        >>> p.restore_default()\n"
"\n"
"        >>> proyecto.cerrar()"

#: aequilibrae/transit/transit_graph_builder.py:49
msgid ""
"Graph builder for the transit assignment Spiess & Florian algorithm.\n"
"\n"
"    :Arguments:\n"
"        **public_transport_conn** (:obj:`sqlite3.Connection`): Connection to the\n"
"        ``public_transport.sqlite`` database.\n"
"\n"
"        **period_id** (:obj:`int`): Period id for the period to be used. Preferred over start\n"
"        and end.\n"
"\n"
"        **time_margin** (:obj:`int`): Time margin, extends the start and end times by\n"
"        `time_margin` ([start, end] becomes [start - time_margin, end + time_margin]), in order\n"
"        to include more trips when computing mean values. Defaults to ``0``.\n"
"\n"
"        **projected_crs** (:obj:`str`): Projected CRS of the network, intended for more\n"
"        accurate distance calculations. Defaults to ``EPSG:3857``, Spherical Mercator.\n"
"\n"
"        **num_threads** (:obj:`int`): Number of threads to be used where possible.\n"
"        Defaults to ``-1`` (using all available threads).\n"
"\n"
"        **seed** (:obj:`int`): Deprecated. No longer in use.\n"
"\n"
"        **geometry_noise** (:obj:`bool`): Deprecated. No longer in use.\n"
"\n"
"        **noise_coef** (:obj:`float`): Deprecated. No longer in use.\n"
"\n"
"        **with_inner_stop_transfers** (:obj:`bool`): Whether to create transfer edges within\n"
"        parent stations. Defaults to ``False``.\n"
"\n"
"        **with_outer_stop_transfers** (:obj:`bool`): Whether to create transfer edges between\n"
"        parent stations. Defaults to ``False``.\n"
"\n"
"        **with_walking_edges** (:obj:`bool`): Whether to create walking edges between distinct\n"
"        stops of each station. Defaults to ``True``.\n"
"\n"
"        **distance_upper_bound** (:obj:`float`): Upper bound on connector distance. Defaults to\n"
"        ``np.inf``.\n"
"\n"
"        **blocking_centroid_flows** (:obj:`bool`): Whether to block flow through centroids.\n"
"        Defaults to ``True``.\n"
"\n"
"        **max_connectors_per_zone** (:obj:`int`): Maximum connectors per zone. Defaults to ``-1``\n"
"        for unlimited.\n"
"    "
msgstr ""
"Constructor de gráficos para la asignación de tránsito del algoritmo de Spiess & Florian.\n"
"\n"
"    :Argumentos:\n"
"        **public_transport_conn** (:obj:`sqlite3.Connection`): Conexión al\n"
"        Base de datos ``public_transport.sqlite``.\n"
"\n"
"        **period_id** (:obj:`int`): ID del período que se utilizará. Preferido al comienzo\n"
"        y final.\n"
"\n"
"        **time_margin** (:obj:`int`): Margen de tiempo, extiende los tiempos de inicio y finalización en\n"
"        `time_margin` ([inicio, fin] se convierte en [inicio - time_margin, fin + time_margin]), en orden\n"
"        para incluir más viajes al calcular los valores medios. El valor predeterminado es ``0``.\n"
"\n"
"        **projected_crs** (:obj:`str`): CRS proyectado de la red, destinado a más\n"
"        cálculos de distancia precisos. El valor predeterminado es ``EPSG:3857``, Mercator esférico.\n"
"\n"
"        **num_threads** (:obj:`int`): Número de subprocesos que se utilizarán siempre que sea posible.\n"
"        El valor predeterminado es ``-1`` (usando todos los hilos disponibles).\n"
"\n"
"        **semilla** (:obj:`int`): obsoleto. Ya no está en uso.\n"
"\n"
"        **geometry_noise** (:obj:`bool`): obsoleto. Ya no está en uso.\n"
"\n"
"        **noise_coef** (:obj:`float`): obsoleto. Ya no está en uso.\n"
"\n"
"        **with_inner_stop_transfers** (:obj:`bool`): si se deben crear bordes de transferencia dentro\n"
"        Estaciones para padres. El valor predeterminado es ``Falso``.\n"
"\n"
"        **with_outer_stop_transfers** (:obj:`bool`): si se deben crear bordes de transferencia entre\n"
"        Estaciones para padres. El valor predeterminado es ``Falso``.\n"
"\n"
"        **with_walking_edges** (:obj:`bool`): si se deben crear bordes para caminar entre distintos\n"
"        paradas de cada estación. El valor predeterminado es \"Verdadero\".\n"
"\n"
"        **distance_upper_bound** (:obj:`float`): Límite superior en la distancia del conector. El valor "
"predeterminado es\n"
"        ``np.inf``.\n"
"\n"
"        **blocking_centroid_flows** (:obj:`bool`): si se debe bloquear el flujo a través de los centroides.\n"
"        El valor predeterminado es \"Verdadero\".\n"
"\n"
"        **max_connectors_per_zone** (:obj:`int`): Máximo de conectores por zona. El valor predeterminado es ``-1``\n"
"        por ilimitado."

#: aequilibrae/transit/transit_graph_builder.py:1130
msgid ""
"Graph edges creation as a Dataframe.\n"
"\n"
"        Edges have the following attributes:\n"
"            - type (:obj:`str`): Either 'on-board', 'boarding', 'alighting', 'dwell',\n"
"              'inner_transfer', 'outer_transfer', 'access_connector', \"egress_connector\" or\n"
"              'walking',\n"
"            - line_id (:obj:`str`): Only applies to 'on-board', 'boarding', 'alighting' and\n"
"              'dwell' edges,\n"
"            - stop_id (:obj:`str`),\n"
"            - line_seg_idx (:obj:`int`): Only applies to 'on-board', 'boarding' and 'alighting'\n"
"              edges,\n"
"            - b_node (:obj:`int`),\n"
"            - a_node (:obj:`int`),\n"
"            - trav_time (:obj:`float`): Edge travel time,\n"
"            - freq (:obj:`float`),\n"
"            - o_line_id (:obj:`str`),\n"
"            - d_line_id (:obj:`str`),\n"
"            - transfer_id (:obj:`str`)\n"
"        "
msgstr ""
"Creación de bordes de gráficos como un marco de datos.\n"
"\n"
"        Los bordes tienen los siguientes atributos:\n"
"            - tipo (:obj:`str`): Ya sea 'a bordo', 'embarque', 'desapareciendo', 'permanencia',\n"
"              'inner_transfer', 'outer_transfer', 'access_connector', \"egress_connector\" o\n"
"              'caminando',\n"
"            - line_id (:obj:`str`): Sólo se aplica a 'a bordo', 'embarque', 'descenso' y\n"
"              bordes 'habitantes',\n"
"            - stop_id (:obj:`str`),\n"
"            - line_seg_idx (:obj:`int`): Sólo se aplica a 'a bordo', 'embarque' y 'descenso'\n"
"              bordes,\n"
"            - b_nodo (:obj:`int`),\n"
"            - un_nodo (:obj:`int`),\n"
"            - trav_time (:obj:`float`): tiempo de viaje al borde,\n"
"            - frecuencia (:obj:`flotante`),\n"
"            - o_line_id (:obj:`str`),\n"
"            - d_line_id (:obj:`str`),\n"
"            - transfer_id (:obj:`str`)"

#: aequilibrae/transit/transit_graph_builder.py:563
msgid ""
"Graph vertices creation as a dataframe.\n"
"\n"
"        Vertices have the following attributes:\n"
"            - node_id (:obj:`int`): Equal to the ``taz_id`` for centroids/origins. Contiguous\n"
"              after,\n"
"            - node_type (:obj:`str`): Either 'stop', 'boarding', 'alighting', 'od', 'origin',\n"
"              or 'destination',\n"
"            - stop_id (:obj:`str`): Only applies to 'stop', 'boarding' and 'alighting' vertices,\n"
"            - line_id (:obj:`str`): Only applies to 'boarding' and 'alighting' vertices,\n"
"            - line_seg_idx (:obj:`int`): Only applies to 'boarding' and 'alighting' vertices,\n"
"            - taz_id (:obj:`int`): Only applies to 'origin', 'destination', and 'od' nodes,\n"
"              ``-1`` elsewhere,\n"
"            - geometry (:obj:`str`): Geometry object in WKB (well known binary).\n"
"        "
msgstr ""
"Creación de vértices de gráficos como marco de datos.\n"
"\n"
"        Los vértices tienen los siguientes atributos:\n"
"            - node_id (:obj:`int`): Igual a ``taz_id`` para centroides/orígenes. contiguo\n"
"              después,\n"
"            - node_type (:obj:`str`): Ya sea 'parada', 'embarque', 'descenso', 'od', 'origen',\n"
"              o 'destino',\n"
"            - stop_id (:obj:`str`): Sólo se aplica a los vértices de 'parada', 'embarque' y 'descenso',\n"
"            - line_id (:obj:`str`): Sólo se aplica a los vértices de 'embarque' y 'descenso',\n"
"            - line_seg_idx (:obj:`int`): Sólo se aplica a los vértices de 'embarque' y 'descenso',\n"
"            - taz_id (:obj:`int`): solo se aplica a los nodos 'origen', 'destino' y 'od',\n"
"              ``-1`` en otro lugar,\n"
"            - geometría (:obj:`str`): Objeto de geometría en WKB (binario bien conocido)."

